 "api_error_status": null,
 "result": "Rules are recorded as deferred functions when the bundle is declared, then replayed against the app at registration.\n\n**Recording (declaration time)**\n- `Bundle.attach_route_rule` (`src/tessel/sansio/bundles.py:413`) validates the endpoint and view name, then calls `self.record(lambda s: s.attach_route_rule(...))`.\n- `Bundle.record` (L224) appends that lambda to `self.deferred_functions`.\n\n**Registration time**\n- `Tessel.register_bundle` calls `Bundle.register(app, options)` (`src/tessel/sansio/bundles.py:273`).\n- `Bundle.register` calls `make_setup_state` (L246) to build a `BundleSetupState`, then loops over `self.deferred_functions` (L334) and calls each with that state.\n\n**Applying (`BundleSetupState`, `src/tessel/sansio/bundles.py:34`)**\n- `BundleSetupState.attach_route_rule` (L87) prepends `url_prefix` to the rule and applies the subdomain and `url_defaults`.\n- It namespaces the endpoint as `\"{name_prefix}.{name}.{endpoint}\"`.\n- It finally calls `self.app.attach_route_rule(...)` (`src/tessel/sansio/app.py:606`), which adds the rule to the app's URL map.\n\nThe concrete `Bundle` in `src/tessel/bundles.py:18` subclasses the sansio one.",
